  m_Name: NewspaperLetter
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Category: 2
  Prefab: {fileID: 6625514644646704096, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  Interactable: {fileID: 5048261325816738630, guid: 1f6a6789373206e498f996cb54aeedb1, type: 3}
  TextFields:
  - "Chicago Standard: Editorial Office \u2014 Print Division"
  - "\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t8/8/2098\nDear Astrid,\r\n\r\nThank you for your letter and
    inquiry, which arrived here by post just before the last delivery cutoff. It\u2019s
    always encouraging to receive thoughtful submissions, especially now\u2014when
    print is not just tradition, but necessity.\r\n\r\nYour story proposal about
    the meteor stood out. The subject is timely, urgent, and deeply personal. We
    believe our readers would be interested, and we would very much like to consider
    it for publication in our August 14 edition.\r\nThat said, a few essential details
    are still missing - especially the timeline. To move forward, we\u2019ll need
    the following:\r\n * A clear timeline of the events you described\r\n * Any available
    supporting documentation (written logs, observational notes, public records,
    etc.)\r\n * A brief explanation of your connection to the satellite project mentioned\u2014this
    is especially important given recent rumors\r\n\nWe know mail is slow and resources
    are limited. But if you can send the missing pieces by the end of the week (Aug
    11), we should be able to include your piece in the next cycle.\r\nThank you
    again for reaching out. The return of thoughtful, grounded reporting is one of
    the few essential in a difficult time\u2014and your voice, if you\u2019re willing,
    could be part of that.\n\nSincerely,\r\nNadine Cho"
  - 'Editor, Print Features

    Chicago Standard

    Print Division, Editorial
    Office

    Sector: Central Lakes / Route: CHI-S3 / Post Node: Press Dock 6'
  StreamingVisuals: []
  DefaultPinnedPos: {x: 0.6, y: 1.5, z: 0}
  ZoomOffsetOverride: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0}
  PreserveInArchive: 1
  TriggersPrompter: 1
